1.1.1 — the mode switch keeps its colours, and the status breathes

Disabling the switch during a recording handed its colours to Windows, which
paints a disabled button's text grey whatever the foreground colour says: the
chosen half turned into dark grey on black and became unreadable. The buttons now
stay enabled and simply refuse to act, which they already did.

The state in the corner carries that job instead. "Recording" is set bold and
breathes between a faded and a full red on exactly the curve the dot in the
notification area uses, so a glance at either says the same thing.

